\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  Curling:  A big old gear shift from an Olympic final that will be spoken of forever in the sport of figure skating to the more sedate curling rink at the water cube. We pick up the Team GB v USA clash with the score still 5-4 in favour of the Brits but John Shuster has the hammer. "He's not the Olympic champion for nothing," says Steve Cram as he blasts Bruce Mouat's shot out of the house. That's two scoreless ends in a row as they move to the ninth. As for Sweden and Canada, they're level 3-3 deep in their eighth; Sweden's Nikilas Edin to go last with work to do and he sneaks it in there. So, the higher-ranked Swedes take a one point lead with two ends to play. }
