\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  Figure skating:  Quad flip into triple toe to start for Shcherbakova and makes it! And another quad flip for good measure. She's away. They're the only quads scheduled, will she adapt and throw in another now in response to Trusova? She doesn't - triple lutz/triple loop comes next - and landed with a smile on her face. Faultless! It might be the case that on any other night, she's winning this. Surely that's silver but it can't overtake Trusova on the free skate alone - she'll need every bit of the six mark buffer she had over her from the short program. All eyes on the judges - "It is going to be so, so close." 171.54 is the required score move into first... and she's done it! 175.75! Shcherbakova snatches the lead by four marks!  And now, to finish, Kamila Valieva, the 15-year-old genius to finish the competition. Performing to Bolero. Strap in. }
